  abstract = {The argument and thought-experiment now generally known as the ChineseRoom Argument was first published in a 1980 article by Americanphilosopher John Searle (1932– ). It has become one of the best-knownarguments in recent philosophy. Searle imagines himself alone in aroom following a computer program for responding to Chinese charactersslipped under the door. Searle understands nothing of Chinese, andyet, by following the program for manipulating symbols and numeralsjust as a computer does, he sends appropriate strings of Chinesecharacters back out under the door, and this leads those outside tomistakenly suppose there is a Chinese speaker in the room.},
